# Antigravity. With a Google-account sign-in, model traffic and account state go to one of the two hosts below,
# chosen by account kind. daily-cloudcode-pa is a production endpoint despite its name.
# - Google's Code Assist page names cloudcode-pa, "an internal API that provides IDE-related features":
#   https://docs.cloud.google.com/gemini/docs/codeassist/set-up-gemini
# - No page that was read names daily-cloudcode-pa or the split. agy's own log under ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/log/
#   shows the split after a consumer sign-in.
# The Business and API-key modes below come from agy's changelog entries 1.1.10 and 1.1.13:
# https://github.com/google-antigravity/antigravity-cli/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md
allow https://cloudcode-pa.googleapis.com/        tunnel  # GCP-licensed accounts
allow https://daily-cloudcode-pa.googleapis.com/  tunnel  # consumer accounts: AI Pro/Ultra/One/Free

# GEMINI_API_KEY, the Gemini API with no sign-in: https://antigravity.google/docs/cli/install
allow https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/  tunnel

# Business sign-in with a Gemini Enterprise license in a Google Cloud project uses two APIs, at the host of the
# license's location:
# - the Business AI Code API, for the license, the configuration and generateContent;
# - the Agent Platform API, which the enterprise doc has the project enable.
# The location is `global`, `us` or `eu`, the doc's whole choice: https://antigravity.google/docs/enterprise
# Business AI Code "provides AI-powered code generation for Antigravity in Gemini Enterprise":
# https://docs.cloud.google.com/gemini/enterprise/docs/ai-developer-tools-settings
# The multi-region hosts: https://docs.cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/docs/learn/locations
# SECURITY.md, "Not defended", has what the aiplatform tunnels open to the credential.
# Advanced WIF sign-in exchanges tokens at sts.googleapis.com and iamcredentials.googleapis.com. That exchange is a
# workspace's own setup: add the host to .ko-agent-sandbox/egress/rule when the proxy's 403 names the host.
allow https://businessaicode.googleapis.com/      tunnel
allow https://aiplatform.googleapis.com/          tunnel  # global
allow https://aiplatform.us.rep.googleapis.com/   tunnel  # us
allow https://aiplatform.eu.rep.googleapis.com/   tunnel  # eu

# Google-account sign-in, consumer and Business alike.
allow https://accounts.google.com/                tunnel  # printed sign-in URL
allow https://oauth2.googleapis.com/              tunnel  # code exchange and token refresh

# Eligibility check. Signed in, agy reads the account at userinfo, then the profile picture at the URL that the
# `picture` field names. A refusal at either host shows agy's "Eligibility check failed" banner, with the model list
# loaded.
# Google constrains `picture` only to a URL, not to a host or path. Google's examples use this host with paths of
# different shapes, so the rule allows the whole host:
# https://developers.google.com/identity/openid-connect/reference
# https://developers.google.com/identity/siwg/security-bundle
# https://developers.google.com/identity/gsi/web/reference/js-reference
allow https://www.googleapis.com/oauth2/v2/userinfo read
allow https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/            read

# `/voice` under --audio=mic streams the recording over gRPC, which needs HTTP/2 and so a tunnel. The proxy refused
# this host in agy 1.3.4's "Could not start transcription" error.
allow https://aicode.googleapis.com/              tunnel

# play.googleapis.com serves telemetry and experiment polling. The host is absent, as ab.chatgpt.com is absent from
# model-provider/openai.
